cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its evaluation protocol, please cite it as below."
title: "World Cup Forecasting Lab: a leakage-tested, prospectively evaluated football forecasting research lab"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Mahmoudimahyar"
    website: "https://github.com/Mahmoudimahyar"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Mahmoudimahyar/Soccer-forcasting"
license: MIT
version: "0.3.0"
date-released: "2026-09-20"
keywords:
  - probabilistic forecasting
  - football
  - calibration
  - Elo rating
  - prospective evaluation
  - negative results
abstract: >-
  A research lab for probabilistic football forecasting (pre-match and in-play) with a fixed evaluator,
  first-write-wins prediction ledgers and machine-readable decision ledgers. Frozen models were scored
  prospectively on 34 fixtures of the 2026 World Cup group stage (an exploratory sample); no model could
  be distinguished from the bookmaker consensus at that sample size, and the market comparator was an
  early line captured a median of about 98 hours before kickoff, not a closing line. Research-only and
  paper-only; no profitability is claimed.
